Downstream patch for @better-auth/oauth-provider 1.8.0-beta.3.

Defect: refresh-token reuse detection does not linearize with rotation. A
rotation revokes its parent and then inserts the child in a separate,
non-transactional write. A concurrent replay of the parent, in another process,
deletes the client/user refresh history (a request-time findMany/deleteMany scan)
between those writes; the paused rotation then inserts a child that remains
usable, including after restart (RFC 9700 section 4.14.2 is not met). The
replay path also skips issuance hooks, and code replay cleanup has the same gap.

Fix: one oauthRefreshFamily row per authorization grant, keyed by the code's
stored identifier (authorizationCodeId). Rotation locks that row and performs
the parent compare-and-swap and child insert in one transaction on the bound
adapter. Reuse, code replay and RFC 7009 revocation revoke the family
permanently by exact key. Refresh grant, refresh introspection and opaque
access-token validation refuse tokens of a revoked, expired or missing family.
No request path enumerates refresh history; expired rows are left to bounded
retention jobs.

Drop this patch once upstream ships equivalent atomic, permanent family
revocation without history scans. Upstream issue draft and reproduction:
services/auth/scripts/probe-native-refresh.ts.
